  message: "PREMISE RE-CHECK 2026-09-29 on dev 6929699126: CURRENT, the count drifted. The re-key is still only in the bare-Name branch (py.py:8557-8571 inside :8290). self.X.save() goes to the Site-3 branch (:8575) and emits python:external:0-0:save (:8662); obj.rel.save() goes to the generic chain branch (:8674+). No attribute-receiver branch calls _is_django_model_instance, though oracle.model_instance() (:5154) can already resolve a forward-relation hop. KNOWN_GAP test test_py_django_setup_fields.py:126 unchanged. Not fixed by WI-lurob/zupiz/nibum/sitos (open) or WI-zamud/sihoh (done, other shapes).\n\nREPRO (Pos.order = ForeignKey(Order)): self.order.save(), o = self.order; o.save(), and self.order.delete() -> external. CONTROLS o = Order.objects.get(); o.save() and self.save() -> django.db.models save, db_write in io-boundaries.\n\npretix re-measured (survey 354 s, 2.1 GB; ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/premise_09292026/kufok/): 1,086 attribute-receiver .save()/.delete() sites, 0 reach django.db.models (812 own external edges, 270 collapse into a caller's single src->external:save edge, 4 resolve to the project's Order.save override). DRIFT: the filed ~1,110 counted refresh_from_db/full_clean, which are not in DJANGO_ORM_INSTANCE_WRITE_METHODS (:886, {save, delete}). Like-for-like: 923 self.<field>.save|delete in src/tests (997 repo-wide) + 89 obj.rel. Some receivers are FieldFiles (item.picture.save), not model instances. The fix must widen both emit sites (Site-3 :8575 and the chain branch :8674), not only the Name branch.\n\nIn passing (not filed): Site-3 stamps inherited_field_receiver on a field the class itself declares (own_field_names reads only __init__) -- overlaps WI-lurob."  # 5279
